{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.48.13.a001", "note": "שִׁיתוּ לִבְּכֶם לְ 'set your heart to' rendered by the idiom 'Mark ye well'; no English word answers to any one morpheme, so the idiom fuses (rule 6), headed on the verb and on 'Mark'. The 2mp suffix is included since 'ye' carries the second-person plural reference; competing reading marks the suffix unrepresented outside the idiom.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.48.13.001", "WLC.PSA.48.13.002", "WLC.PSA.48.13.003", "WLC.PSA.48.13.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.48.13.001", "status": "noncompositional", "target": ["t001", "t002", "t003"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "PSA.48.13.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.48.13.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.48.13.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "PSA.48.13.a003", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.48.13.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.48.13.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "PSA.48.13.a004", "note": "Margin 'Traverse' read and set aside (rule 38).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.48.13.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.48.13.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "PSA.48.13.a005", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.48.13.008"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.48.13.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "PSA.48.13.a006", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.48.13.009"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.48.13.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "PSA.48.13.a007", "note": "Purpose לְמַעַן takes the complementizer 'That'.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.48.13.010"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.48.13.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "PSA.48.13.a008", "note": "Verb takes subject pronoun and modal (rule 17).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.48.13.011"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.48.13.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010", "t011", "t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "PSA.48.13.a009", "note": "S